{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rev16: both cutover(3388) and DC-robustness(5c0e) down to a single blocking finding each; iterating.\n- 3388 G6 (verified against origin/main): my rev15 step-3 wrongly routed the emit compare's REMOTE through normalize_outbound, which would break the load-bearing once-only legacy-body upgrade (outbound_field_diff.py:287-291 / outbound_fields.py:555-561 deliberately compare raw-remote to force a one-time re-emit). Root insight: the emit compare at :292 ALREADY has both operands in decoded space (fitted=normalize_outbound(fit(local)) vs canonical_remote=decode(wire) via inbound_mapper at :188), so a lossy round-trip already cancels there WITHOUT re-normalizing — and re-normalizing would kill the upgrade. The genuine lossy misfire is only in the BASELINE compares (_suppressed_by_inbound:252, _local_matches_baseline:385), which compare RAW local vs decoded baseline. Fix: normalize only the LOCAL side of those two; leave emit compare (:292) and _remote_matches_baseline (:399) unchanged. rev17 applied (9 AC).\n- 5c0e G1G2 (verified): adding reconciler.dc_pandoc_timeout_s requires the full reconciler.* config surface (mirrors jira_cli_timeout): _config_schema.py field+validator, _config_sources.py optional env alias, tests/golden/config_surface.json, docs/config.md, plus a config-file-wiring test. Added to Scope + file_impact. rev17 applied (3 AC)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785817417071263001,"uuid":"3bf92731-8726-469d-8c36-c13b0126999b"}